{
  "chapter.756FE2AA913E8F06.title": "04 • DynEco: Trade and Play",
  "task.4A789DED52D7441A.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.3828E5DDA0C35009.title": "Start here: DynEco",
  "quest.3828E5DDA0C35009.quest_subtitle": "Start Here",
  "quest.3828E5DDA0C35009.quest_desc": [
    "DynEco adds an in-game market with simulated buyers, listings and changing prices. It helps turn surplus production into purchasing power. Gamble It is connected by your local addon to this same wallet; there is no separate deposit currency.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/economy.png width:330 height:150 align:center}",
    "",
    "&b&lChoose a branch&r",
    "• First Transactions",
    "• Factory Exports",
    "• Optional Casino",
    "",
    "Your route: tablet and power -> inspect prices -> a small purchase and sale -> linked storage and automation -> wallet checks -> optional casino rules. No quest requires a gambling win.",
    "",
    "&eStart with the first equipment milestone, then follow the branch you need."
  ],
  "task.2341213D399DE802.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.00762979529AB361.title": "Map legend & completion rules",
  "quest.00762979529AB361.quest_subtitle": "Reference",
  "quest.00762979529AB361.quest_desc": [
    "Follow a branch that solves your next problem. Equipment icons lead to concrete inventory milestones; the book card is a reference, and a large diamond marks a workshop project.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the setup before crafting. Item milestones detect your inventory without consuming items. Their practical checkmarks are optional reminders; final workshop projects require a practical confirmation. An item in your bag does not prove that a machine is configured. Existing equipment counts: do not rebuild a working system just for this map.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "JEI shows this pack's current recipes. Branches explain how the systems connect. Optional side projects are independent of the main route; no casino win is required."
  ],
  "task.2151F8A945A8C6C4.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.4C37D18D9440A483.title": "Craft the Market Tablet",
  "quest.4C37D18D9440A483.quest_subtitle": "First Transactions",
  "quest.4C37D18D9440A483.quest_desc": [
    "The tablet is the market interface. It needs energy, so crafting it alone is not enough to start trading.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Craft the Market Tablet with the current JEI recipe. Charge it in an FE charger, or use its supported redstone-block charging interaction, then right-click with it to open the market.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If the interface does not open, check charge and the item's tooltip before changing economy settings."
  ],
  "task.12212E99DDB3B78A.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.4C47ACFC848D1DA7.title": "Know your wallet",
  "quest.4C47ACFC848D1DA7.quest_subtitle": "First Transactions",
  "quest.4C47ACFC848D1DA7.quest_desc": [
    "A wallet balance is purchasing power, not inventory space. New DynEco accounts use the configured starting balance; this guide grants no extra credits.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect your balance in the tablet and compare it with /dyneco balance. Note the display currency and base-credit value before testing transactions.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The casino always uses whole base credits. A different DynEco display currency can make the displayed numbers look different without changing the underlying money."
  ],
  "task.4C5267F1A558E7A2.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0DEDA51D16462441.title": "Read a price before buying",
  "quest.0DEDA51D16462441.quest_subtitle": "First Transactions",
  "quest.0DEDA51D16462441.quest_desc": [
    "The broad market includes many machines and tools. A listed base item price is not a valuation of its enchantments, stored contents or upgrades.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Search a common resource and inspect its current buy/listing information. Compare a few related materials and choose an inexpensive test purchase.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Start with plain resources and empty replaceable machines. Do not use a unique upgraded tool as your first market experiment."
  ],
  "task.5A185C4B75A1632A.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.31A9161E3C2D2100.title": "Your first small purchase",
  "quest.31A9161E3C2D2100.quest_subtitle": "First Transactions",
  "quest.31A9161E3C2D2100.quest_desc": [
    "A tiny purchase lets you verify price, quantity, payment and delivery before committing a large balance.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Buy a small quantity of an ordinary material. Check the confirmation, wallet change and delivered items. Locate the items before making a second order.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Read quantities carefully. If a transaction seems delayed, inspect the current screen and order state rather than repeatedly clicking buy."
  ],
  "task.573D8366E379BB5B.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.364B51AEDAF9422C.title": "List a surplus item",
  "quest.364B51AEDAF9422C.quest_subtitle": "First Transactions",
  "quest.364B51AEDAF9422C.quest_desc": [
    "Selling to simulated buyers is not the same as instantly exchanging every stack for cash. Listings may need time to find buyers.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "List a small surplus stack of a common resource. Record the starting balance and quantity, then inspect the listing after time passes and confirm an actual sale.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Unsold listings are not earned credits. Keep materials needed for your next machine outside the first experiment."
  ],
  "task.69314B40D0BCEDF3.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.79902E2AE165400C.title": "Supply, demand and patience",
  "quest.79902E2AE165400C.quest_subtitle": "First Transactions",
  "quest.79902E2AE165400C.quest_desc": [
    "Dynamic prices reward checking the market. Flooding one item or buying a large quantity can behave differently from a single small transaction.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Observe the same item across a few ordinary trades. Compare demand, available supply and the displayed price without assuming a fixed sell value forever.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "DEMAND IS SHARED: /marketlimits shows your remaining total and category allowances. Recovery is $10,000 per online hour overall; bulk $500, farming $1,500, resources $4,000 and manufactured goods $10,000, all inside that shared total. Extra chests do not create extra buyers.",
    "",
    "PRICE EXAMPLE: Neutral cobblestone base value is $0.01 and a diamond pickaxe is about $352.02. A normal spread makes the pickaxe roughly $457.63 to buy and $246.42 to sell before demand changes. The market rounds a batch, not every fractional-cent unit.",
    "",
    "EXPENSIVE GOODS: Per-item/bucket buyback ceilings are $250 bulk, $750 farming, $2,000 resources and $5,000 manufactured. High compression keeps retail value but does not guarantee a good resale deal. Check the displayed sell quote.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use the market to support your progression. A price derived from recipes is not a hand-balanced appraisal of every ATM10 machine."
  ],
  "task.3E95692AA58A91DE.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3C3E8D6ACBA66724.title": "Link a storage chest",
  "quest.3C3E8D6ACBA66724.quest_subtitle": "Factory Exports",
  "quest.3C3E8D6ACBA66724.quest_desc": [
    "Linked storage makes repeated transfers easier, but the chosen chest should contain only the goods you intend to trade.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place a dedicated trade chest and sneak-right-click it with the tablet to link it. Verify the selected storage and test with a few low-value items before setting automation.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Name or label the chest. Keeping your workshop's only tools in a trading chest is an easy way to sell something you still need."
  ],
  "task.50F979C1AEB65D9F.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5A1FB2CD3C301F4B.title": "Automate one export",
  "quest.5A1FB2CD3C301F4B.quest_subtitle": "Factory Exports",
  "quest.5A1FB2CD3C301F4B.quest_desc": [
    "Automatic selling is most useful for genuine surplus from a renewable production line.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Configure one ordinary item for automatic selling from the linked storage. Feed it a small batch, observe listings and completed sales, and check the resulting wallet change.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "TWO BUFFERS: Production fills your personal reserve first; only surplus enters the trade chest. Choose one resource and record wallet plus chest quantity, wait for a completed sale, then compare both. A listing is not income until it settles.",
    "",
    "AFTER THE LIMIT: Remaining goods should wait. Allowance refills only while online and persists across reconnects. Saved demand supports a later burst, so a single large sale is different from a sustainable hourly income.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep a reserve upstream. Let your production fill a buffer before diverting surplus to the trade chest.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/economy.png width:330 height:150 align:center}"
  ],
  "task.1C37BEBB130DD2D2.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7928D79F2D94447D.title": "Buy to a budget",
  "quest.7928D79F2D94447D.quest_subtitle": "Factory Exports",
  "quest.7928D79F2D94447D.quest_desc": [
    "Automatic buying should solve a known shortage without consuming the balance reserved for other projects.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the tablet's automatic-buy controls and configure a small bounded requirement if suitable controls are available. Otherwise use manual purchases. Verify the item and storage destination.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not enable an open-ended buying rule just to complete a quest. The goal is a predictable supply cost."
  ],
  "task.3967F4125DDECAE3.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.17036B4B0B368140.title": "When an item is missing",
  "quest.17036B4B0B368140.quest_subtitle": "Factory Exports",
  "quest.17036B4B0B368140.quest_desc": [
    "The broad-market rules still exclude selected creative/admin items and honor DynEco's deny lists. Some resources can also lack useful pricing data.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Check the item's exact ID with advanced tooltips and search again. If you have permission, /dyneco why <item_id> and /dyneco price <item_id> can explain eligibility or pricing.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A missing market entry does not mean the item is absent from the pack. JEI and the mod's normal progression remain available."
  ],
  "task.26275FBEBAD938C9.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5D7DB41591DF03FD.title": "Project: a modest trade loop",
  "quest.5D7DB41591DF03FD.quest_subtitle": "Factory Exports",
  "quest.5D7DB41591DF03FD.quest_desc": [
    "A useful economy setup has a clear input, retained reserves, sales and a practical purchase at the end.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Produce a renewable resource, keep a reserve, sell a small surplus and spend part of the proceeds on something your next project needs. Confirm that your remaining balance matches your expectations.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "This is the main economy capstone. Everything below is an optional casino guide and is not required for the trading workflow."
  ],
  "task.7A5D1018661F5D74.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.4DEC0220AF3FA45F.title": "Optional: open the casino",
  "quest.4DEC0220AF3FA45F.quest_subtitle": "Optional Casino",
  "quest.4DEC0220AF3FA45F.quest_desc": [
    "Gamble It provides several chance-based games. In this profile, the wallet bridge makes bets and winnings change DynEco directly.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Press F8 with the default CustomATM key binding while in a world with menus closed. If reassigned, search Open Casino under Casino Mod in Controls. Open the interface, identify the shared DynEco balance, and close it without placing a bet.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "OPENING: The CustomATM default casino key is F8. If you changed it, search Open Casino under Casino Mod in Controls. The casino uses the same server-side DynEco wallet; you do not need to buy or deposit a separate token.",
    "",
    "OPTIONAL BRANCH: These quests do not require wins, repeated bets or a particular balance. Use a small amount you already intend to spend for entertainment. Closing the interface is a valid end to the session.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "One casino credit equals one DynEco base credit; fractional cents stay in the wallet. The original item deposit/shop is disabled. Buy and sell through the Market Tablet."
  ],
  "task.3FD0CB86F3CE64EA.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.454FFCC7287165A0.title": "Optional: read a game first",
  "quest.454FFCC7287165A0.quest_subtitle": "Optional Casino",
  "quest.454FFCC7287165A0.quest_desc": [
    "A game's rules and payout display tell you what the selected stake means. Different games do not offer the same outcomes.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Open Coin Flip or Slots and inspect the bet controls, rules and displayed results. You can complete this reading task without placing a bet.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A losing result is normal gameplay, not proof that the wallet bridge is broken. No strategy here promises profit."
  ],
  "task.5947CBD76805B5D2.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.754777A9B561B904.title": "Optional: staged rounds",
  "quest.754777A9B561B904.quest_subtitle": "Optional Casino",
  "quest.754777A9B561B904.quest_desc": [
    "Mines, Blackjack and Crash involve choices during a round. Their in-game cash-out controls remain available even though the separate item shop is disabled.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the chosen game's instructions and locate its round controls before starting. If you play, finish the round while connected and then inspect the wallet.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Gamble It discards unfinished sessions on logout without a refund. Close out active rounds before leaving the world."
  ],
  "task.06DA44C1F2641025.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.2EF47CB2F277BA8F.title": "Optional: a tiny wallet test",
  "quest.2EF47CB2F277BA8F.quest_subtitle": "Optional Casino",
  "quest.2EF47CB2F277BA8F.quest_desc": [
    "A controlled test checks integration without making a win a progression requirement.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "If you want to play, choose the smallest accepted stake and finish one round. Compare the wallet before and after, accounting for the displayed payout. Otherwise inspect the rules and acknowledge that you skipped the wager.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Market sales can also change the balance while the casino is open. Use a quiet test period when checking the arithmetic."
  ],
  "task.4359BBA9ED6B5AFD.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.077709C3169232DC.title": "A useful stopping point",
  "quest.077709C3169232DC.quest_subtitle": "Factory Exports",
  "quest.077709C3169232DC.quest_desc": [
    "The economy and casino share money. A budget for entertainment is separate from the resources you need to finish your colony or workshop.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Choose a reserve for your next practical build and keep it available. Return to trading, crafting or exploration after your chosen session; the guide has no repeated betting or jackpot requirement.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If you need a repair, report the game, stake, before/after base-credit balance and whether automatic sales were active."
  ],
  "task.36E1EBA88A4550A1.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.1249F36A0A74EF6C.title": "Benchmark a bulk export",
  "quest.1249F36A0A74EF6C.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • First Transactions",
  "quest.1249F36A0A74EF6C.quest_desc": [
    "A cobble generator can outproduce simulated buyer demand by many orders of magnitude. Its value is a low-effort trickle, not an unlimited source of spending money.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Record /marketlimits and your wallet, offer 64 cobble, and inspect the completed payout. Feed more into the same trade buffer and compare the price and available bulk demand after sales.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Bulk demand recovers at $500 per online hour inside the $10,000 shared total. A full buffer can simply wait for demand; adding chests does not increase the allowance."
  ],
  "task.051A247EE91931AF.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.07BBDE484D583500.title": "Resources have their own market",
  "quest.07BBDE484D583500.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Factory Exports",
  "quest.07BBDE484D583500.quest_desc": [
    "Processed resources earn more per item than common blocks but remain automatable through farms and ore-processing chains.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Offer a small iron surplus while retaining your construction reserve. Compare the resource allowance and total allowance before/after a completed sale, then contrast it with the cobble experiment.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The resource category recovers at $4,000 per online hour. Those credits are part of the shared total, not an extra allowance added on top."
  ],
  "task.5B9EC7AEA43CABDE.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3CE45445CD716967.title": "Price a finished product",
  "quest.3CE45445CD716967.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Factory Exports",
  "quest.3CE45445CD716967.quest_desc": [
    "A finished product has a recipe cost and an opportunity cost: selling its ingredients separately may produce a different result. Machines should be manufactured to a useful plan rather than blindly crafted for sale.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Compare the current diamond pickaxe buy and sell quotes with the ingredients. Make or inspect one plain pickaxe, calculate the expected margin, and choose whether selling it makes sense. The quest does not require you to sell it.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Enchantments, damage and stored contents are not a guaranteed premium. Keep unique equipment out of an automated sale chest."
  ],
  "task.347C67F9F1DC5DBB.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3AAC3B4EA5336F69.title": "Production comes before exports",
  "quest.3AAC3B4EA5336F69.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Factory Exports",
  "quest.3AAC3B4EA5336F69.quest_desc": [
    "An export buffer should be downstream of your own stock requirement. Otherwise a fast selling system can empty the resources needed to expand the factory.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Label one chest Reserve and the other Exports. Use your preferred logistics mod to maintain a modest reserve and send only overflow to Exports. Connect only Exports to the market and test with inexpensive blocks.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The SFM and XNet chapters both teach bounded transfers. Pick one controller for this job so competing rules do not fight over the same items."
  ],
  "task.45C819E6AAB438AA.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3D680F81B6FF8F43.title": "Compression changes quantity, not demand",
  "quest.3D680F81B6FF8F43.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • First Transactions",
  "quest.3D680F81B6FF8F43.quest_desc": [
    "One iron block represents nine ingots. High compression can make transport easier, but it cannot multiply your per-player buyer allowance.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Compare the block and ingot sell quotes before moving valuable compressed stock. Read the category buyback ceiling in /marketlimits and decide which form is sensible to offer. Keep the block if the quote is poor.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Very expensive compressed blocks can hit the per-item ceiling. Buying one and unpacking it for resale is not a substitute for checking actual prices and limited demand."
  ],
  "task.6BB95F5F95E50C59.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.66E8AABE6566F2EC.title": "A factory you can budget",
  "quest.66E8AABE6566F2EC.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Factory Exports",
  "quest.66E8AABE6566F2EC.quest_desc": [
    "Useful balance is measured over time. One large sale after stored demand accumulated does not establish what the factory earns continuously.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use a Book and Quill to record starting wallet, purchases, payouts, elapsed online time and /marketlimits. Observe a normal session and compare net earnings with the resources you actually consumed.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The target is around $10,000/hour for a developed factory, not a guaranteed payment. Market demand and product choices can put actual earnings below the ceiling."
  ]
}
